SAIF AI — SOFTWARE LICENCE
==========================

Copyright (c) SAIF AI. All rights reserved.

This document is the licence for SAIF AI, the Android application in this
repository. It is written to be read by a person, not only by a lawyer.


1. WHAT THIS COVERS
-------------------

This licence covers everything SAIF AI wrote: the application source in
`app/src/main/java/com/example/**` (the `ui`, `llm`, `agent`, `studio`,
`saifagent`, `saifcore`, `saiflive`, `live`, `stt`, `builder`, `compiler`,
`terminal`, `cloud`, `data`, `github`, `audio`, `utils` and `util`
packages), the `apprunner` module, the local workspace daemon in
`termux-daemon/`, and the build scripts and documentation in this
repository.

If you want to hand SAIF AI to someone else so they can put their own name
and their own licence on it, use `SAIF_AI_OWNERSHIP_AND_RELICENSING.md`.
Fill in their name, sign it, and it is theirs.

Each of those source files carries a notice naming SAIF AI as the copyright
holder. Where a file carries no such notice, it is a third-party component
and is governed by the licence named for it in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`
instead of by this document.


2. OWNERSHIP
------------

SAIF AI owns this software. Every part of it was written for SAIF AI: the
structure, the names, the logic and the arrangement are SAIF AI's own. No
part of it is a copy, a translation, or a rearrangement of somebody else's
program.

Where SAIF AI's code once had to work alongside code belonging to other
projects, that code has been removed and replaced with SAIF AI's own
implementations. `LICENSE_AUDIT.md` records how that was measured rather
than asserted.


3. WHAT YOU MAY DO
------------------

You may use SAIF AI. Install it, run it, use it to build things.

You may read the source. It is published so that what the app does is not a
secret, so that it can be reviewed, and so that the people who distribute it
can show exactly what they are distributing.


4. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO
----------------------

You may not redistribute SAIF AI, or a modified version of it, without
written permission from SAIF AI.

You may not sell it, publish it to an app store under your own name, or
offer it as a service to other people.

You may not present it as your own work. The copyright notice in each source
file must be left where it is.

You may not remove or hide the third-party notices in
`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`. Those components do not belong to SAIF AI, and
their terms travel with them.

The name SAIF AI, and the SAIF AI marks and iconography, are not licensed by
this document.


5. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
-------------------------

SAIF AI is built on work published by other people under open licences.
Those components keep their own licences, which are listed, with the
dependency that pulls each one in, in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`. That file
also states which of them are copyleft and what, if anything, that requires
of anyone distributing the application.

Nothing in this document overrides the licence of a third-party component.


